Moreover, by [ChP1, Proposition 1], we have that the elements $t_{1},\ldots, t_{n}, X_{1},\ldots, X_{n}$ form a commutative family, that is,
\begin{equation}
xy=yx\quad\mathrm{for~any}~x,y\in \{t_{1},\ldots, t_{n}, X_{1},\ldots, X_{n}\}.\label{xyyx}
\end{equation}
