\end{equation}
Then it is proved in [ChP1, Lemma 1] that we have, for any $1\leq i\leq n-1$,
\begin{equation}
g_{i}X_{j}=X_{j}g_{i}\quad\mathrm{for}~j=1,2,\ldots,n~\mathrm{such~that}~j\neq i, i+1.\label{giXj}
\end{equation}
Moreover, by [ChP1, Proposition 1], we have that the elements $t_{1},\ldots, t_{n}, X_{1},\ldots, X_{n}$ form a commutative family, that is,
