\right.
\end{align*}\vspace{0.2cm}
For simplicity, we write $(i_1, i_2, i_3)$ instead of $((\nu_{i_1}, \nu_{i_2}, \nu_{i_3}),(j_{i_1}, j_{i_2}, j_{i_3}))$ or $(j_{i_1}, j_{i_2}, j_{i_3}).$ We need to check that $\tau_{1}\tau_{2}\tau_{1}1_{(\nu, j)}=\tau_{2}\tau_{1}\tau_{2}1_{(\nu, j)}.$ Then there are four cases for consideration.
